      "content": "You cut off again right at the end there—you were saying \"ensure that she has access to clean...\"? Please finish that thought.\n\nAlso, thanks for the list. I'm still a bit uneasy about this \"swelling or heat\" part. Since the infection would be deep inside her abdomen, how do I actually distinguish between a normal post-op inflammatory response and something more sinister, like a localized abscess or peritonitis? It feels like something could be lurking or festering in those dark, hidden spaces in her rumen and I wouldn't even know until it's too late. Are there any specific subtle changes, like a particular smell or a certain type of abdominal pain, that would hint at a hidden intruder of an infection? I just need to be sure I catch it immediately.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
